  "summary_en": "Sweden's 2026 national AI strategy sets the goal of ranking among the world's top ten AI nations. It stresses regulatory simplification, public-sector AI use, computing infrastructure, skills, language models, security and defence. It supports regulatory sandboxes and standards, and EU simplification of the AI Act. It has almost no robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Aims for Sweden to be a top-ten AI nation",
   "Pushes EU regulatory simplification and delay of new AI legislation until standards exist",
   "Supports regulatory sandboxes and AI standards as alternatives or complements to legislation",
   "Creates a public-sector AI workshop, fully operational by 2030",
   "Public-sector AI must ensure transparency, traceability and appealability of decisions"
